note as DEP_diagram_48_automation
  Connects to other modules via:
  directory.tenants, iam.users (agents.acts_as_user_id — automated writes are attributable),
  integrations.integration_endpoints (agent_tools), platform_ops.service_components,
  common.files (knowledge_sources), messaging.domain_events (automation_triggers consume the
  event bus; runs enqueue via module 35), authz.permissions (tool permission_effect),
  terminology.catalog_concepts. record_automations write to ANY target schema under guardrails.
end note

note as REC_GOVERNANCE_diagram_48_automation
  ATTRIBUTION & GOVERNANCE
  Every automated write sets created_by_user_id/updated_by_user_id to agents.acts_as_user_id
  (a dedicated service identity) and is journaled to audit with the agent_run_id as source.
  Write-capable tools with requires_approval=true MUST pass through automation_approvals
  (human-in-the-loop) before executing. guardrail_policies bound PII/PHI handling and cost.
end note

note as REC_DERIVED_diagram_48_automation
  REC 3.3 — DERIVED
  workflow_runs.total_cost_amount and agent_runs token/cost fields roll up from
  agent_run_steps (append-only). agents.current_version / workflows.current_version track the
  latest published version. agent_memory may expire (TTL).
end note

note as HARDENING_diagram_48_automation
  REC 3.4 — HARDENING (enforce at DDL)
  - agent_run_steps: append-only; PARTITION BY recorded_at; index (agent_run_id, sequence_no).
  - agent_tool_bindings: UNIQUE(agent_version_id, agent_tool_id).
  - automation_approvals: pending write actions block tool execution until status='approved'.
  - record_automations: dedupe by dedupe_key_expr to avoid duplicate record creation.
  - polymorphic (target_resource_type/context_ref_type/scope_ref_id,*_ref_id) -> value_set + trigger.
end note

note as VALUE_SETS_diagram_48_automation
  VALUE SETS (bind *_concept_id; do not hardcode)
  agent_type->vs_agent_type{llm,rule_based,rpa,hybrid,human_proxy};
  autonomy_level->vs_autonomy{suggest_only,human_approval,supervised,autonomous};
  tool_type->vs_agent_tool_type{db_read,db_write,http_call,search,notify,compute,handoff};
  orchestration_type->vs_orchestration{sequential,parallel,dag,state_machine,router};
  step_type/step_kind->vs_step_kind{agent_call,tool_call,condition,human_task,wait,transform};
  trigger_type->vs_trigger_type{event,schedule,webhook,manual,record_change};
  automation_action->vs_automation_action{create,update,enrich,validate,route,classify,summarize,extract};
  write_mode->vs_write_mode{draft,direct,upsert};
  approval_type->vs_approval_type{write,external_call,high_cost,phi_access};
  memory_type->vs_memory_type{episodic,semantic,procedural,scratch};
  scope->vs_memory_scope{global,tenant,workflow,entity};
  policy_type->vs_guardrail_type{content,cost,rate_limit,phi,tool_allowlist};
  enforcement->vs_enforcement{block,warn,log};
  pii_phi_handling->vs_phi_handling{deny,mask,allow_with_consent};
  source_type(knowledge)->vs_knowledge_source{document,url,table,vector_index};
  status/state->vs_lifecycle_state.
end note


